  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "2002 (March) U.S. Echo Integration-trawl Survey Data for Walleye Pollock (Theragra chalcogramma) on the Shelikof Strait Area, the Shelf Break Area near Chirikof Island, and Barnabas Trough (Cruise ID: MF2002-04)",
  "description": "Echo integration-trawl (EIT) survey was carried out between 12 and 26 March, 2002, in the Shelikof Strait area, off the Gulf of Alaska shelf break east of Chirikof Island, and in Barnabas and Chiniak Troughs. Samples were collected from one bottom trawl and twenty-eight midwater trawl hauls. Pollock catch data include distribution, relative abundance, size composition, sex ratio and maturity. Other data include biomass estimates, acoustic data, echosign data, temperature/depth profiles, conductivity-temperature-depth (CTD) observations, sea surface temperature, salinity, and ocean current profile. Cruise ID: MF2002-04 (March 12-26, 2002) Survey vessel: NOAA Ship R/V Miller Freeman For cruise results see http://www.afsc.noaa.gov/race/surveys/cruise_archives/cruises2002/results_MF2002-04.pdf\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: To assess the abundance and distribution of walleye pollock in the Gulf of Alaska.",
  "url": "https://zenodo.org/records/23513803",
